    <div class="warn">
      <b>What this page could not verify:</b> four things. (1) Where <b>693</b> comes from. The safe accepts it in every recording that gets that far, and the handle goes green on exactly that value, but none of our four videos shows the clue that produces it — the numbers on the plant stands are the obvious candidate and the mapping is never demonstrated. (2) What the <b>nine-button weather panel</b> at 6:50 is for. It lights up, the pictograms are legible, and no item, counter or compartment follows in any recording; we are not going to invent a rule for it. (3) What the <b>Modified hanger</b> and the <b>Screwdriver</b> are actually used on. Both go into the bag and both are still there at the end, so the only honest statement is that they are a pair the game hands you without showing you the target. (4) The payout. The <b>+5 coins</b> and <b>14:10</b> come from a recording whose build labels this room <b>Level 24</b> — the same furniture, the same codes, different numbering — so the first-clear reward on the Level 20 build may be larger than +5. Everything else here — 693, 12:08, 12850, 02851, the receipt lines, the red-to-green reader and the item names — was read off the screen at least twice.
